From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc: drop nonexistent gpl.texi auxiliary input

The tagged source archive does not contain doc/gpl.texi, and macchanger.texi
does not include it. Do not ask Automake to distribute a nonexistent file.

Root cause: tag 1.7.0 declares an auxiliary Texinfo input that is absent from
the official archive even though the main manual does not reference it.
Patch-Source: downstream reconstruction from the official 1.7.0 archive
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are prohibited)
Removal: remove when a stable upstream release stops declaring doc/gpl.texi.

---
 doc/Makefile.am | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/Makefile.am b/doc/Makefile.am
--- a/doc/Makefile.am
+++ b/doc/Makefile.am
@@ -2 +1,0 @@
-macc_TEXINFOS = gpl.texi
--
2.50.1
